# St. Leopold's Asylum: The Abyss of Mind

A first-person psychological horror game that runs entirely in your browser. Explore a decaying psychiatric hospital, recover four missing patient files, scavenge weapons and supplies, and survive whatever is hunting you in the dark. The hallways do not stay where you left them.

Built with plain HTML, JavaScript and [Three.js](https://threejs.org/). There is no build step and no install.

---

## Quick start

1. Download `the_abyss_of_mind_upgraded.html`. Rename it to `index.html` if you plan to host it.
2. Open it in a modern desktop browser (Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Safari).
3. Click **ENTER CLINICAL WING**, then click on the game once so it has keyboard focus.

> **Internet connection required.** The game loads Three.js, Tailwind CSS, Font Awesome and Google Fonts from CDNs.

### Hosting on GitHub Pages

1. Rename the game file to `index.html` and push it to your repository.
2. Go to **Settings → Pages**.
3. Set the source to your main branch and the root folder, then save.
4. Your game will be live at `https://<your-username>.github.io/<repo-name>/`.

---

## Objective

Find all **4 patient records** scattered across the hospital wings. Read each one with **E**. Collect the fourth to complete the game.

You start unarmed in the bright clinical wing. The deeper wings are dark, bloodstained and dangerous. Search the desks for weapons and look for batteries, ammo and medical supplies along the way.

---

## Controls

| Action | Keys |
|---|---|
| Move | `W` `A` `S` `D` |
| Sprint | `Shift` (uses stamina) |
| Look | Arrow keys or `I` `J` `K` `L` (the mouse also works) |
| Turn around instantly | `X` |
| Attack | Left mouse click |
| Flashlight | `F` |
| Examine or pick up | `E` |
| Open or close the map | `M` |
| Equip weapons | `1` Fists, `2` Scalpel, `3` Fire Axe, `4` Handgun (or mouse wheel) |
| Reload handgun | `R` |
| Explore Mode (invulnerable) | `G` |

