## Features

### Realistic hallways
- Narrow, hospital-scale corridors with a low ceiling.
- Procedurally generated textures: plaster walls above glossy tile wainscoting, chair rails, baseboards, grime, water stains and blood drips.
- Ward doors with frames, windows and number plates.
- Scuffed checker linoleum floors, stained acoustic-tile ceilings and blood pools.
- Props: gurneys (some with a sheeted body), wheelchairs, bins, rusted pipes, glowing EXIT signs and drifting dust.

### Lighting
- Dozens of fluorescent fixtures, with only the nearest few casting real light, so it stays smooth.
- Dead and flickering lights in the dark wings.
- Random power blackouts.
- An offset flashlight that lags behind your aim, flickers when the battery runs low, and flashes when you fire the handgun.

### Survival mechanics
- Health, sprint stamina and a flashlight battery that drains over time.
- Pickups: batteries, ammo and medical supplies.
- Three weapons with different range and damage: Scalpel, Fire Axe and Handgun (with reload and reserve ammo).
- Combat is aim-based and needs line of sight. You cannot hit things behind you or through walls.
- Rats scatter from you, and some of them bite.
- A death screen when your health reaches zero.

### The Stalker
- A pale patient that patrols the hospital using real pathfinding.
- It sees your flashlight, hears you when you sprint, and slows down when you shine your light on it.
- It cannot be killed for good. When it falls, it gets back up somewhere else after a while.
- It sleeps until you have explored a bit, and it gets faster as you recover more records.
- A heartbeat and a rising drone warn you when it is close.

### A map that will not stay still
- **Timed changes:** the layout rewrites itself every 15 to 45 seconds, starting after about 40 seconds of play. Walls open and close out of your sight.
- **Progress changes:** each record you find triggers another change and makes things worse. The lights die, the fog thickens, the bright wing darkens and reddens, and the Stalker speeds up.
- **Safe by design:** changes never trap you or cut the map into disconnected pieces, and they never remove pickups.
- **Shifting corridors:** two corridors swap places when you whip around quickly.
- **Live blueprint map:** the **M** map shows the current layout, but it warns you when it is out of date.

### Accessibility and fairness
- **Explore Mode (`G`)** makes you invulnerable so you can look around freely.
- Keyboard-only play: movement, looking and turning around all work without a mouse.
- If the browser blocks mouse capture (for example in an embedded preview), the game still starts, and on-screen movement buttons appear if no key presses are detected.
- A red banner shows any script error, which makes bugs easier to report.

